{
  "sticker": "caterpillar",
  "skeleton": "caterpillar seen from the side, head raised on the left: a chain of bones from the tail segment (root, on the ground at the right) through the body segments to the head, so it can ripple, rear up and curl; antennaL/antennaR on the head; face with eyes and mouth.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a caterpillar character. Draw this exact caterpillar as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the head: the big round green-and-yellow head, facing left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks; no antennae.\n2. one antenna: a green antenna with its round tip.\n3. the first body segment behind the head: pale yellow in front and green behind, with its little legs below.\n4. the second body segment, with its spots and little feet.\n5. the third body segment, with its spots and little feet.\n6. the last tail segment, with its spots and little feet.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a caterpillar character; image 2 shows the same caterpillar cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the caterpillar's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the caterpillar in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the caterpillar's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a big dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n9. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
